## My Experience

Karel was one of my first experiences with algorithmic thinking.

Some problems initially looked simple, but solving them for different world sizes made me think more carefully about my approach. I gradually learned that writing a working program is not just about making it run once, but about understanding why it works.

These exercises helped me build the foundation I needed before moving on to Python.

